SUMMARY:FYI: What’s happenin’
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nFor Oct 14 thru Oct 21\n\nUpcoming **music 
 events** may be found here:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/\n(Up
 dates on Thurs morning)\n\n**Assorted entertainment\, festival & market ev
 ents may be found here:**\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/calendar-of-e
 vents\n\n**Library programs** may be found here:\nhttps://hendersonpl.libc
 al.com/\n\n**Wednesday\, October 14**\nJason DeCristofaro's Jazz Night\n6-
 8pm\, Southern Appalachian Brewery\, 822 Locust St\, Hendersonville\n\n**W
 ednesday\, October 14**\nWeekly Westie Wednesdays (Ages 21 & Up) (Each Wed
 nesday)\n7-10pm\, Honeysuckle Holler\, 101 East Allen St\, Suite 101\, Hen
 dersonville NC 28792\n7-8pm - Continuation Lesson & 7:30-8pm - Beginner Le
 sson. 8-10pm - Social Dance.\nLessons rotate weekly with our incredible in
 structor lineup: Ryan Pflumm\, Jason Barnes\, Jenna Shimek\,\nMissy Lindse
 y\, Rachel Harris\, Tom and Janet Leazenby\, and Tola Sun - all bringing f
 resh energy and\nperspectives each week! Enjoy a rotation of community DJs
  keeping the vibes high and the floor full all night\nlong. No outside dri
 nks (including water bottles) - water station available. Outside food welc
 ome. Dress is\ncasual and No partner needed! Dedicated parking next to the
  venue & street parking. Please help us\nsupport our amazing host venue by
  grabbing a drink or snack at the bar - it helps keep dance nights thrivin
 g!\nPricing: $10 lesson & social\, $5 social only.\n\n**October 15th**\n**
 Rhythm & Brews:**\n5:30 pm - 9:00 pm\; Free\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc
 .org/\nPresented by Horizon Heating & Air\, Rhythm & Brews Concert Series 
 brings together live music\, local craft beverages\, and the community! Th
 ese free shows take place on the third Thursday of every month from June-O
 ctober\, closing part of South Main Street to make room for all the fun. L
 ocal food trucks will line the street cooking delicious eats from kettle c
 orn to pizza to barbecue. Each show begins with an opener at 5:00 p.m. fol
 lowed by the headlining performance from 7:00-9:00 p.m.\n2026 Rhythm & Bre
 ws Concert Series Lineup:\nOctober 15: Unspoken Tradition [[Bluegrassl] wi
 th Finkelstein Three [[Bluegrass/Jazzgrass]]\nOpening acts will kick off e
 ach evening at 5 p.m. followed by the headliner performance from 7-9 p.m.\
 n\n**October 16 thru 18th\; 10a - 4p**\n***Open Studio Tour 2026***\nFor o
 ne weekend\, visitors will have the opportunity to meet artists where they
  create\, see works in progress\, learn about different creative processes
 \, and discover original artwork and handmade pieces throughout the region
 . While the tour is rooted in Henderson County\, some participating artist
 s have studios just beyond the county line.\nhttps://www.studio116nc.com/s
 tudiotour\n***Maps & locations TBD***\n\n**October 17** @ 10:30 am - 4:00 
 pm\nOrchard Days: Harvest & Handmade Market\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc
 .org/event/orchard-days-harvest-handmade-market\nhttps://justusorchard.com
 /\n\nOctober 17\; 2-5 PM\nSOUTHER WILLIAMS VINEYARD \\* Autumnwüd \\* 2:0
 0 – 5:00\n\n**October 18** @ 3:00 pm - 5:00 pm\; $12\nThe Hendersonville
  Community Band will play the first concert of our new season on October 1
 8 at 3PM at the Blue Ridge Community College. Theme is Fall Colors. There 
 will be a variety of selections. We will feature Furman University student
  Jillian Hansard – a clarinet soloist & Hendersonville Community Band sc
 holarship winner on “Clarinet Candy”. Holst’s “Second Suite in F
 ”\, Clifton Williams’s “Symphonic Suite”\, “Pixar Movie Magic”
 \, John Williams’s “Chillers and Thrillers” (Halloween!)\, Sousa’s
  march “The Thunderer” (with guest conductor Mr. James Phillips from H
 endersonville High School). Lastly\, a trumpet trio on “Carnival Variati
 ons” – something for everyone! Advance tickets available at Hendersonv
 ille Visitors Center. Tickets are $12 (students free) and also available a
 t door.\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/hendersonville-community-
 band-fall-colors-concert\n\n**Tuesday\, October 20**\nMountain Shag Club D
 ance\n6:30-9pm\, The Mule at Devil's Foot Beverage\, 131 Sweeten Creek Rd\
 , Ste 10\, Asheville NC 28803\nCost: $7 per person.\n\n**Wednesday\, Octob
 er 21**\nJason DeCristofaro's Jazz Night\n6-8pm\, Southern Appalachian Bre
 wery\, 822 Locust St\, Hendersonville\n\n**Oct 22**\nCroquet & Bocce ball 
 at Jackson Pk\nOct & Nov schedule\nhttps://www.hendersoncountync.gov/recre
 ation\n\n**Oct 23 & 24\; 9am – 2 pm**\n**Hospice Warehouse sale\;.**\nht
 tps://www.facebook.com/HospiceHomeStore\n\n**Wednesday\, October 21**\nJas
 on DeCristofaro's Jazz Night\n6-8pm\, Southern Appalachian Brewery\, 822 L
 ocust St\, Hendersonville\n\n**Wednesday\, October 21**\nCarolina Shag Nig
 ht - Featuring DJ Rick Selimos (Open to the Public)\n6-9pm\, American Legi
 on Post 88\, 115 East Morgan St\, Brevard NC 28712\n6-6:30pm - Free Shag D
 ance Lesson. 7-9pm - Dancing to DJ Rick Selimos who will be playing a mix 
 of\nShag\, Swing\, Slow Dance and Line Dance music.\n\n**Wednesday\, Octob
 er 21**\nWeekly Westie Wednesdays (Ages 21 & Up) (Each Wednesday)\n7-10pm\
 , Honeysuckle Holler\, 101 East Allen St\, Suite 101\, Hendersonville NC 2
 8792\n7-8pm - Continuation Lesson & 7:30-8pm - Beginner Lesson. 8-10pm - S
 ocial Dance.\nLessons rotate weekly with our incredible instructor lineup:
  Ryan Pflumm\, Jason Barnes\, Jenna Shimek\,\nMissy Lindsey\, Rachel Harri
 s\, Tom and Janet Leazenby\, and Tola Sun - all bringing fresh energy and\
 nperspectives each week! Enjoy a rotation of community DJs keeping the vib
 es high and the floor full all night\nlong. No outside drinks (including w
 ater bottles) - water station available. Outside food welcome. Dress is\nc
 asual and No partner needed! Dedicated parking next to the venue & street 
 parking. Please help us\nsupport our amazing host venue by grabbing a drin
 k or snack at the bar - it helps keep dance nights thriving!\nPricing: $10
  lesson & social\, $5 social only.\n\n**October 24\;** Free\nGHOULFEST IS 
 COMING!\nGet ready for a spooky Sunday at Ecusta Market Cafe & Trailside B
 rewing Co. on October 24th\, 11AM–5PM!\n35+ local vendors\nLive music wi
 th Kate Bryant 12–2PM + Josh Dunkin 3–5PM\nSpooky scavenger hunt\; Cos
 tume contest\; Face painting\nCold drinks + good food\nAnd plenty of Hallo
 ween fun!\n441 S Whitted St\, Hendersonville\, NC\nhttps://visithendersonv
 illenc.org/event/halloween-goulfest-at-trailside-brewing\n\n**October 24**
  @ 6:00 pm - 9:00 pm\; Free\nParker’s Back Vintage Jazz at Trailside Bre
 wing\nJoin us for an evening of timeless tunes and toe-tapping rhythms wit
 h Parker’s Back\, a string trio bringing vintage vocal jazz\, swing\, an
 d Gypsy Jazz classics to life — from the 1920s onward.\nFeaturing:\nRobb
 ie Grice – guitar & vocals\; Alex Travers – violin\; James Dawkins –
  upright bass\nWhether you’re a fan of Django-style swing\, smooth jazz 
 standards\, or just looking for a fun night out\, you’ll love the energy
  and charm of this WNC-based trio.\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/even
 t/parkers-back-vintage-jazz-at-trailside-brewing\n\n**Fri\; Oct 23**\n**Ho
 spice Warehouse sale\; Oct 23 & 24. (**(3rd Fri/Sat of mnth)\nYou'll find 
 a wide variety of value furniture items at the warehouse. Shop with us eac
 h month when we host our 2-day warehouse sales and support the care servic
 es of Four Seasons.\n9:00 AM - 2:00 PM\; 561 S Allen Rd\, Flat Rock\nhttps
 ://www.facebook.com/HospiceHomeStore\n\n**Saturday\, October 24**\nThe Sho
 wboat Band\n6-9pm\, Bold Rock Hard Cidery\, 72 School House Rd\, Mills Riv
 er\n\n**Saturday\, October 24**\nMountain Shag Club Halloween Party (With 
 DJ Tommy Samole)\n6-10pm\, Hendersonville Elks Lodge\, 546 North Justice S
 t\, Hendersonville NC 28739\nCostume Contest and bring a snack to share. F
 REE for members and $10 for Guests.\n\n**Saturday\, October 24**\nFine Lin
 e\n6-10pm\, J&M Farms\, 3016 Chimney Rock Road\, Hendersonville\n\n**Sunda
 y\, October 25**\nHendersonville Ballroom Dance Club Tea Dance - Dress: La
 tin look – Fringe or Ruffles\n3-5:30pm\, Upstairs at Hedrick Rhodes Vete
 rans Center\, 900 North Main St\, Hendersonville NC 28792\n3pm - Cha Cha D
 ance Lesson with Carrie Fernandez.\nAmple parking at the front entry of th
 e building\, take the elevator or stairs to the upper level. Parking is\nl
 imited at the rear entrance\, both front and back doors will be unlocked. 
 3-5:30pm - Open Ballroom Dance to\nthe music of DJ Gary Bills. Our dances 
 are open to the public and everyone is invited. Enjoy Ballroom\nDancing to
  the music of DJ Gary Bills who plays a variety of dance tunes including S
 wing (East & West\nCoast)\, Waltz\, Tango\, Rumba\, Cha-Cha and Foxtrot. T
 here is also a dance mixer Cost: $5 per person at\ndoor.\n\n**Sunday\, Oct
 ober 25**\nPeggy Ratusz @ SAB\; 6PM\nSouthern Appalachian Brewery\; 822 Lo
 cust St. Hendersonville\n\nThese are NOT hosted events and are posted for 
 informational purposes only. Please make personal arrangements to meetup w
 ith friends and family.\nIf you wish to attend and host one of these event
 s\, I will post the event as an individual happening. Hosting only require
 s being focal point for others and making introductions. Simple!!
