SUMMARY:Panthertown Great Wall Loop\; the hike.
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nPanthertown Valley\, often referred to as t
 he Yosemite of the East\, visitors can enjoy deep gorges and broad valleys
 \, mountain bogs and granitic rock domes\, tranquil creeks and plunging wa
 terfalls. Panthertown Valley is protected as part of the Panthertown-Bonas
  Defeat bear sanctuary.\nRough terrain trails lead to 3 waterfalls and “
 the Great Wall’ pluton. Exceptional views.\n**Difficulty:** Immediate 30
 0 ft descent into the valley. Short\, steep descents to the base(s) of 3 w
 aterfalls. Staircase-steep climb (400ft) to the top of the Great Wall Plut
 on followed by a steep descent. Natural surfaced trails with rocks & roots
 . 2 ea rock-hop stream xings (possibly wet). The last mile to the cars is 
 a 300 ft ascent.\nMountain Trolls are thieves\; Zip your backpacks tight.\
 nWe are the ***HFF Trail Trekkers***: We a’gonna get our step-counters a
 ’workin’ !!\nHugh will lead\; Up to 12 ppl are welcome to join.\n**PAR
 TICIPANTS REQUIRE THE APPROVAL OF THE HIKE ORGANIZER.**\nHike Details:\n**
 Wagon Train rolls at 9:30AM**\nHike Distance: 6.0 mi (feels like 7.5)\; Ac
 cum ascent: 1200 ft\; Pace: 2.0 mph\; Elevation: 4000ft\n**Drive time: 1 h
 r/33 mi 1-way**\n**Trkhd: “Panthertown Valley trailhead” (Salt Rock Tr
 ailhead)**\n**GPS:** 35.168599\,-83.040279\n**Return Not earlier than: 3 P
 M (=5.75 hrs)**\n**Carpool contributions appreciated. $5.00 suggested**\nW
